## 4\. Correct action execution and receipts

Route manual controls, keyboard, touch and voice through dispatchUiAction\.

Preserve named structured arguments\. Validate schema, target existence, capability, permission, current manifest version and idempotency before executing\. Never flatten JSON into a pseudo\-function string\.

Each operation returns:

```ts
interface ActionReceipt {
  actionId: string;
  runId: string;
  status: 'accepted' | 'running' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'blocked' | 'cancelled';
  targetId: string | null;
  buildId: string;
  stateVersion: number;
  observedState: Record<string, unknown>;
  errorCode?: string;
  evidence?: Record<string, unknown>;
}
```

“Completed” requires the expected state to be observed\. Examples: the panel is mounted, the camera has arrived, the video frame is presented, or the requested PDF page texture is uploaded\. A queued tour returns “started/running”, never “tour completed”\.

Reject stale target IDs and re\-read the current registry\. Unknown operations fail honestly with available alternatives\. Gemini may propose allowlisted typed actions; it may not inject arbitrary HTML, execute code, select arbitrary DOM nodes or bypass server permissions\.

